================================================================== 600 1451
  Definition of Data                                               600 1451
================================================================== 600 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                 600 1451
================================================================== 600 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction.  600 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a        600 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons  600 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).               600 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between    600 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative      600 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                             600 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be   600 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,      600 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically      600 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                       600 1451
