==================================================================1100 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         1100 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          1100 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  Contents                                                        1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  Warning                                                         1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 1100 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist1100 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  Definition of Data                                              1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 1100 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       1100 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 1100 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              1100 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   1100 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     1100 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            1100 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  1100 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     1100 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     1100 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
  References                                                      1100 1451
==================================================================1100 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 1100 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   1100 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 1100 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 1100 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 1100 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    1100 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        1100 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    1100 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       1100 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     1100 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          1100 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             1100 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                1100 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         1100 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            1100 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               1100 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         1100 1451
