==================================================================2300 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                2300 1451
==================================================================2300 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 2300 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       2300 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 2300 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              2300 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   2300 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     2300 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            2300 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  2300 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     2300 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     2300 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      2300 1451
