==================================================================2800 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 2800 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       2800 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 2800 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              2800 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   2800 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     2800 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            2800 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  2800 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     2800 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     2800 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      2800 1451
