----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 3000                               3000 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       3000 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         3000 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          3000 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  Contents                                                        3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  Warning                                                         3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 3000 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist3000 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  Definition of Data                                              3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 3000 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       3000 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 3000 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              3000 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   3000 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     3000 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            3000 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  3000 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     3000 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     3000 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  References                                                      3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 3000 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   3000 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 3000 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 3000 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 3000 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    3000 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        3000 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    3000 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       3000 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     3000 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          3000 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             3000 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                3000 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         3000 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            3000 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               3000 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         3000 1451
                                                                  3000 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library3000 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   3000 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   3000 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
  History                                                         3000 1451
==================================================================3000 1451
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         3000 1451
 (2) November, 2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       3000 1451
 (3) September,2014 - Insure Standard C, C++, FORTRAN Format      3000 1451
 (4) September,2014 - Updated based on recently publshed data     3000 1451
 (5) September,2017 - New Binding Energies (see: ref.3)           3000 1451
                      Same Transition Probabilities               3000 1451
 (6) August,   2023 - Reformatted, but data same as 2017 version  3000 1451
