----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 4200                               4200 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       4200 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         4200 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          4200 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
  Contents                                                        4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
  Warning                                                         4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 4200 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist4200 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
  Definition of Data                                              4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                4200 1451
==================================================================4200 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 4200 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       4200 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 4200 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              4200 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   4200 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     4200 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            4200 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  4200 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     4200 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     4200 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      4200 1451
