==================================================================4600 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                4600 1451
==================================================================4600 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 4600 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       4600 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 4600 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              4600 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   4600 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     4600 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            4600 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  4600 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     4600 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     4600 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      4600 1451
==================================================================4600 1451
  References                                                      4600 1451
==================================================================4600 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 4600 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   4600 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 4600 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 4600 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 4600 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    4600 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        4600 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    4600 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       4600 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     4600 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          4600 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             4600 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                4600 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         4600 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            4600 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               4600 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         4600 1451
                                                                  4600 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library4600 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   4600 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   4600 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               4600 1451
==================================================================4600 1451
  History                                                         4600 1451
==================================================================4600 1451
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         4600 1451
 (2) November, 2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       4600 1451
 (3) September,2014 - Insure Standard C, C++, FORTRAN Format      4600 1451
 (4) September,2014 - Updated based on recently publshed data     4600 1451
 (5) September,2017 - New Binding Energies (see: ref.3)           4600 1451
                      Same Transition Probabilities               4600 1451
 (6) August,   2023 - Reformatted, but data same as 2017 version  4600 1451
