----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 4700                               4700 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       4700 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         4700 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          4700 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  Contents                                                        4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  Warning                                                         4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 4700 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist4700 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  Definition of Data                                              4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 4700 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       4700 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 4700 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              4700 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   4700 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     4700 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            4700 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  4700 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     4700 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     4700 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
  References                                                      4700 1451
==================================================================4700 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 4700 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   4700 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 4700 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 4700 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 4700 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    4700 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        4700 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    4700 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       4700 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     4700 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          4700 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             4700 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                4700 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         4700 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            4700 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               4700 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         4700 1451
                                                                  4700 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library4700 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   4700 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   4700 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               4700 1451
