----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 5200                               5200 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       5200 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         5200 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          5200 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  Contents                                                        5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  Warning                                                         5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 5200 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist5200 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  Definition of Data                                              5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 5200 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       5200 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 5200 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              5200 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   5200 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     5200 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            5200 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  5200 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     5200 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     5200 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
  References                                                      5200 1451
==================================================================5200 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 5200 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   5200 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 5200 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 5200 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 5200 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    5200 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        5200 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    5200 1451
