  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                5700 1451
==================================================================5700 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 5700 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       5700 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 5700 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              5700 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   5700 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     5700 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            5700 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  5700 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     5700 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     5700 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      5700 1451
==================================================================5700 1451
  References                                                      5700 1451
==================================================================5700 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 5700 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   5700 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 5700 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 5700 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 5700 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    5700 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        5700 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    5700 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       5700 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     5700 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          5700 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             5700 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                5700 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         5700 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            5700 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               5700 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         5700 1451
                                                                  5700 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library5700 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   5700 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   5700 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               5700 1451
==================================================================5700 1451
  History                                                         5700 1451
==================================================================5700 1451
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         5700 1451
 (2) November, 2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       5700 1451
 (3) September,2014 - Insure Standard C, C++, FORTRAN Format      5700 1451
 (4) September,2014 - Updated based on recently publshed data     5700 1451
 (5) September,2017 - New Binding Energies (see: ref.3)           5700 1451
                      Same Transition Probabilities               5700 1451
 (6) August,   2023 - Reformatted, but data same as 2017 version  5700 1451
