 58-Ce-  0 NDS,IAEA   Eval-Aug23 D.E.Cullen                       5800 1451
 NDS-IAEA-224         Dist-Jan25                                  5800 1451
----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 5800                               5800 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       5800 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         5800 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          5800 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  Contents                                                        5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  Warning                                                         5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 5800 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist5800 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  Definition of Data                                              5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 5800 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       5800 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 5800 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              5800 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   5800 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     5800 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            5800 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  5800 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     5800 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     5800 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  References                                                      5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 5800 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   5800 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 5800 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 5800 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 5800 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    5800 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        5800 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    5800 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       5800 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     5800 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          5800 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             5800 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                5800 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         5800 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            5800 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               5800 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         5800 1451
                                                                  5800 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library5800 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   5800 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   5800 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
  History                                                         5800 1451
==================================================================5800 1451
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         5800 1451
 (2) November, 2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       5800 1451
 (3) September,2014 - Insure Standard C, C++, FORTRAN Format      5800 1451
 (4) September,2014 - Updated based on recently publshed data     5800 1451
 (5) September,2017 - New Binding Energies (see: ref.3)           5800 1451
                      Same Transition Probabilities               5800 1451
 (6) August,   2023 - Reformatted, but data same as 2017 version  5800 1451
