----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 5900                               5900 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       5900 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         5900 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          5900 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  Contents                                                        5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  Warning                                                         5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 5900 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist5900 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  Definition of Data                                              5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 5900 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       5900 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 5900 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              5900 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   5900 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     5900 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            5900 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  5900 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     5900 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     5900 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
  References                                                      5900 1451
==================================================================5900 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 5900 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   5900 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 5900 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 5900 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 5900 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    5900 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        5900 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    5900 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       5900 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     5900 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          5900 1451
