----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 6100                               6100 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       6100 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         6100 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          6100 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  Contents                                                        6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  Warning                                                         6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 6100 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist6100 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  Definition of Data                                              6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 6100 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       6100 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 6100 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              6100 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   6100 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     6100 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            6100 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  6100 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     6100 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     6100 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  References                                                      6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 6100 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   6100 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 6100 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 6100 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 6100 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    6100 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        6100 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    6100 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       6100 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     6100 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          6100 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             6100 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                6100 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         6100 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            6100 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               6100 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         6100 1451
                                                                  6100 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library6100 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   6100 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   6100 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
  History                                                         6100 1451
==================================================================6100 1451
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         6100 1451
 (2) November, 2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       6100 1451
 (3) September,2014 - Insure Standard C, C++, FORTRAN Format      6100 1451
 (4) September,2014 - Updated based on recently publshed data     6100 1451
 (5) September,2017 - New Binding Energies (see: ref.3)           6100 1451
                      Same Transition Probabilities               6100 1451
 (6) August,   2023 - Reformatted, but data same as 2017 version  6100 1451
