----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 6200                               6200 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       6200 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         6200 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          6200 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  Contents                                                        6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  Warning                                                         6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 6200 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist6200 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  Definition of Data                                              6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 6200 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       6200 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 6200 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              6200 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   6200 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     6200 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            6200 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  6200 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     6200 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     6200 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
  References                                                      6200 1451
==================================================================6200 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 6200 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   6200 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 6200 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 6200 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 6200 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    6200 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        6200 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    6200 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       6200 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     6200 1451
