----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 7600                               7600 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       7600 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         7600 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          7600 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  Contents                                                        7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  Warning                                                         7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 7600 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist7600 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  Definition of Data                                              7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 7600 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       7600 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 7600 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              7600 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   7600 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     7600 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            7600 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  7600 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     7600 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     7600 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
  References                                                      7600 1451
==================================================================7600 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 7600 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   7600 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 7600 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 7600 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 7600 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    7600 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        7600 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    7600 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       7600 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     7600 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          7600 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             7600 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                7600 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         7600 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            7600 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               7600 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         7600 1451
                                                                  7600 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library7600 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   7600 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   7600 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               7600 1451
