  Warning                                                         8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 8900 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist8900 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
  Definition of Data                                              8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 8900 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       8900 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 8900 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              8900 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   8900 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     8900 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            8900 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  8900 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     8900 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     8900 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
  References                                                      8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 8900 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   8900 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 8900 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 8900 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 8900 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    8900 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        8900 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    8900 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       8900 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     8900 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          8900 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             8900 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                8900 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         8900 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            8900 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               8900 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         8900 1451
                                                                  8900 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library8900 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   8900 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   8900 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
  History                                                         8900 1451
==================================================================8900 1451
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         8900 1451
 (2) November, 2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       8900 1451
 (3) September,2014 - Insure Standard C, C++, FORTRAN Format      8900 1451
 (4) September,2014 - Updated based on recently publshed data     8900 1451
 (5) September,2017 - New Binding Energies (see: ref.3)           8900 1451
                      Same Transition Probabilities               8900 1451
 (6) August,   2023 - Reformatted, but data same as 2017 version  8900 1451
