  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 9500 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist9500 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  9500 1451
==================================================================9500 1451
  Definition of Data                                              9500 1451
==================================================================9500 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                9500 1451
==================================================================9500 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 9500 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       9500 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 9500 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              9500 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   9500 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     9500 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            9500 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  9500 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     9500 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     9500 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      9500 1451
==================================================================9500 1451
  References                                                      9500 1451
==================================================================9500 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 9500 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   9500 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 9500 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 9500 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 9500 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    9500 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        9500 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    9500 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       9500 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     9500 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          9500 1451
4) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2017: April 2019 Status Report",             9500 1451
   IAEA-NDS-228, April 2019, Nuclear Data Section,                9500 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         9500 1451
5) D.E. Cullen,"EPICS2023: August 2023 Status Report",            9500 1451
   IAEA-NDS-242, August 2023, Nuclear Data Section,               9500 1451
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria.                                         9500 1451
                                                                  9500 1451
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library9500 1451
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   9500 1451
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   9500 1451
  of the data, etc.                                               9500 1451
==================================================================9500 1451
  History                                                         9500 1451
==================================================================9500 1451
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         9500 1451
 (2) November, 2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       9500 1451
 (3) September,2014 - Insure Standard C, C++, FORTRAN Format      9500 1451
 (4) September,2014 - Updated based on recently publshed data     9500 1451
 (5) September,2017 - New Binding Energies (see: ref.3)           9500 1451
                      Same Transition Probabilities               9500 1451
 (6) August,   2023 - Reformatted, but data same as 2017 version  9500 1451
