----ENDF/B-VI         MATERIAL 9700                               9700 1451
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       9700 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         9700 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          9700 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  Contents                                                        9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  Warning                                                         9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 9700 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist9700 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  Definition of Data                                              9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 9700 1451
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       9700 1451
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 9700 1451
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              9700 1451
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   9700 1451
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     9700 1451
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            9700 1451
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  9700 1451
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     9700 1451
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     9700 1451
   calculates these spectra.                                      9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
  References                                                      9700 1451
==================================================================9700 1451
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 9700 1451
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   9700 1451
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 9700 1451
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 9700 1451
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 9700 1451
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    9700 1451
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        9700 1451
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    9700 1451
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       9700 1451
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     9700 1451
